<title>INDIA: India ABB buys stake in Bombay firm.</title>
<headline>India ABB buys stake in Bombay firm.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-05-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Asea Brown Boveri Ltd (ABB) said on Saturday it has acquired a 51 percent equity stake in Bombay-based Lenzohm Electrical Engineering Company.</p>
<p>Lenzohm is engaged in repair and maintenance of electrical machinery which supplements ABB's operations in electricity generation, transmission and distribution and industrial and building systems.</p>
<p>The new company will be called ABB Lenzohm Service Limited, ABB said in a statement.</p>
<p>ABB also has production facilities in Bangalore, Calcutta, Vadodara, Faridabad, Nashik and Madras.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
